    "['xconnect [peer_ip] [vc_id] encapsulation [encapsulation_type] pw-class [pw_class_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ccc', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ccc\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 1.1.1.9 interface ge-1/0/0 virtual-circuit-id 100\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper configuration uses two commands to achieve the same functionality as Cisco's single `xconnect` command\\n- The first command sets the interface to use CCC (Circuit Cross Connect) family\\n- The second command establishes the L2 circuit with the remote peer (1.1.1.9) and specifies the virtual circuit ID (100)\\n- The `pw-class VPWS` aspect is implicitly handled by Juniper's L2 circuit implementation with MPLS encapsulation being the default\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ccc'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 1.1.1.9 interface ge-1/0/0 virtual-circuit-id 100', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ccc\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 1.1.1.9 interface ge-1/0/0 virtual-circuit-id 100\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper configuration uses two commands to achieve the same functionality as Cisco's single `xconnect` command\\n- The first command sets the interface to use CCC (Circuit Cross Connect) family\\n- The second command establishes the L2 circuit with the remote peer (1.1.1.9) and specifies the virtual circuit ID (100)\\n- The `pw-class VPWS` aspect is implicitly handled by Juniper's L2 circuit implementation with MPLS encapsulation being the default\", 'trans_templat